ABSTRACT

This whitepaper presents the QUENNE Stacked Intelligence architecture—a nine‑layer cognitive framework designed for the Orbital Star Ring Smart City, a self‑governing toroidal habitat in low Earth orbit. The architecture aligns ethical governance, nuclear‑domain specialisation, multi‑model cognitive fusion, adaptive resource scaling, hybrid photonic‑electronic computing, physical engineering optimisation, quantum‑inspired algorithms, open‑source operating foundations, and cross‑platform hardware abstraction into a single, vertically integrated intelligence stack.

We demonstrate that cognition in large‑scale space infrastructures need not be centralised; rather, it emerges from the strict layering and tight alignment of specialised subsystems, each certified to the highest safety and reliability standards. The Orbital Star Ring serves as both a proof‑by‑construction and an operational template for future extraterrestrial habitats, lunar bases, and Martian colonies.

This work was developed in collaboration with DeepSeek AI Research Technology, whose large‑language‑model capabilities accelerated system architecture synthesis, interface formalisation, and verification campaign planning.

