5. SYSTEM INTEGRATION ARCHITECTURE

5.1 Communication Backbone

The Star Ring employs a dual‑plane network:

Plane Technology Purpose Determinism
A TTEthernet (AS6802) Hard real‑time control (reactor, attitude) <1 µs jitter
B 10 GbE + Kafka Bulk data, management, world model Best effort

Both planes share the same counter‑rotating fibre ring via DWDM.

5.2 Inter‑Layer API Discipline

All inter‑layer communication is defined in Protocol Buffers v3, with gRPC as the primary synchronous transport. Critical real‑time paths use TTEthernet raw frames.

Example – Ethical Audit API (Protobuf):

```protobuf
message AuditRequest {
    string action_id = 1;
    string layer = 2;
    map<string, Value> params = 3;
    WorldModel context = 4;
}
service Triad {
    rpc Audit(AuditRequest) returns (AuditResponse);
}
```

5.3 Time Synchronisation

· Global time reference: GPS‑disciplined oscillator + chip‑scale atomic clock.
· Distribution: IEEE 802.1AS (gPTP) over TTEthernet.
· Accuracy: <100 ns between any two nodes.

