6. IMPLEMENTATION METHODOLOGY

6.1 Development Paradigm

We adopt Model‑Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) with SysML v1.7 as the single source of truth. All interfaces, state machines, and data flows are captured in the model; code and documentation are generated via automated transformations.

Toolchain:

· Modeling: Cameo Systems Modeler
· Code Generation: BridgePoint (UML to C++), custom XSLT for protobuf
· Build: Bazel (polyglot), Yocto (Linux images), Vitis (FPGA)
· Verification: SPARK, TLA⁺, Coverity, UVM (hardware)

6.2 Simulation Environment

A high‑fidelity digital twin of the entire Star Ring runs on ground and in orbit (on Triad’s strategic node). Components:

· Physics Engine: Bullet Physics + custom orbital dynamics, FEM thermal/structural.
· Sensor Emulation: Realistic noise models for 100,000+ virtual sensors.
· Network Emulation: ns‑3 with TTEthernet and wireless models.
· Full Stack Deployment: The entire QUENNE stack runs inside the simulation, enabling end‑to‑end testing without hardware.

