9. ETHICAL AND SOCIETAL IMPLICATIONS

9.1 Human‑AI Governance

The Triad is designed to augment, not replace, human decision‑making. Residents can petition the Triad for policy changes; referenda are conducted with privacy‑preserving voting. The system includes a “red button” – a physical switch in each segment that reverts control to a minimal safe mode pending ground intervention.

9.2 Transparency

All non‑proprietary code is open source. The ethical rule set is published and subject to international review. An independent ethics board, composed of residents and external experts, audits Triad decisions quarterly.

9.3 Long‑Term Evolution

The QUENNE stack is designed to be amendment‑capable. As societal values evolve, the ethical rule set can be updated through a formal constitutional process.

